id: ops-073p
title: "Docstring coverage gate: a lexer-backed, fail-closed documentation gate the fleet can share"
description: "pm-ops becomes the home of the fleet's documentation gate. Today no repo has one: the mandate requires full docstring coverage on all source, and the only attempt (an unmerged pm-changelog branch) is a line-regex scanner whose own header claims compiler-API rigor it does not have, leaves its internal-function rule unimplemented, and counts braces inside strings and template literals. Implement the analyzer once here, on the TypeScript lexer that ships with the repo's existing typescript devDependency, and expose it both as a pm-ops subpath export the other packages can call from a ten-line script and as a fleet-wide command."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: "area:quality-gate",docstrings,fleet-wide,"pkg:pm-ops"
created_at: "2026-07-30T21:51:52.205Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-31T10:45:52.729Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-31T10:45:52.712Z"
completed_at: "2026-07-31T10:45:52.712Z"
claim_principal: "harness:codex"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "A docstrings module is exported from pm-ops, backed by createScanner token streams rather than line regexes, so JSDoc inside strings, template literals and commented-out code can never satisfy it; every declaration form the finder does not recognise is reported as a violation rather than skipped; the internal-function rule is implemented rather than documented; negative-control tests prove the gate fails on each known-bad input; pm ops docstrings runs the same analyzer across one repo or the fleet; pm-ops passes its own gate"
resolution: "Published the shared analyzer subpath and fleet command, enforced documentation in release/CI, fixed every verified Greptile and CodeRabbit correctness finding across three exact-head rounds, and retained nonzero format-correct failure behavior."
expected_result: "A lexer-backed analyzer and pm ops docstrings command evaluate supported TypeScript declaration surfaces fail-closed, resist misleading comment/string/template inputs, operate across repositories, and pass pm-ops release gates."
actual_result: "116 tests pass with 0 failures and 0 skips, including installed-CLI and live pm-todos/pm-csv acceptance. Docstrings are 85/85, production audit is clean, pack/changelog gates pass, Node 22/26 CI is green, and Greptile is green on the final code head. The separate 100/100/100/100 source-coverage gap remains explicitly open as ops-q6ki."
notes[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-31T09:59:20.024Z","harness:codex","PR 33 has 10 unresolved threads. Implement all verified Greptile and CodeRabbit findings,regenerate the changelog that fails both CI jobs,and rerun the complete release gate before requesting exact-head reviews."
  "2026-07-31T10:20:21.519Z","harness:codex","Complete real-data release gate passes: 113 tests,0 failures,0 skips; pm-todos/pm-csv scan 2/2 ready; pm-csv nested release gate 1/1 passed; docstrings 85/85; production audit 0 vulnerabilities; pack and changelog checks pass. Source coverage remains 94.32% lines,78.45% branches,and 95.04% functions,so the separate mandatory 100/100/100/100 gap is tracked as ops-q6ki and is not being misrepresented as complete."
  "2026-07-31T10:35:03.436Z","harness:codex","Exact-head review round found and resolved two additional fail-closed edge cases: semicolon-free exported variable statements now stop at valid ASI declaration boundaries,and source traversal tracks canonical directories to terminate symlink cycles. Full opted-in release gate now passes 115 tests with 0 failures and 0 skips; coverage is 94.40% lines,78.66% branches,and 95.04% functions,still honestly tracked by ops-q6ki."
  "2026-07-31T10:42:32.092Z","harness:codex","Third exact-head remediation classifies CloseBraceToken as expression-ending,closing object-literal bypasses for exported variables and class fields and correcting slash-as-division tokenization. Full opted-in release gate passes 116 tests with 0 failures and 0 skips; coverage is 94.41% lines,78.68% branches,and 95.04% functions,with the 100% gap still tracked by ops-q6ki."
